<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoàng Ngũ Phúc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1713">1713</a>–<a href="/years/1776">1776</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Hoang Ngu Phuc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoàng Ngũ Phúc was a general of the Trịnh lords who ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Taking advantage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a> rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a>, he led a Trịnh army south and captured the Nguyễn capital Phú Xuân in 1775, briefly extending Trịnh rule over the centre of the country before his death the following year.</p></div>
